        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "This earns a place because the birthday is doing real editorial work: Vereen turns 80 inside a one-night retrospective built around the Broadway, film and television repertoire through which he helped shape American musical theater, and NJPAC is surrounding him with several generations of major stage voices plus the Andy Farber Orchestra. The lineup makes the evening less a solo nostalgia show than a live handoff among performers connected to the same theater-song lineage. It is a strong cultural-history catch inside a jazz festival without pretending that Broadway is suddenly the center of RADAR.",
